{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/807028-bloodline-based-on-camazotz","id":807028,"title":"Bloodline based on Camazotz","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T08:13:51-08:00","id":807028,"title":"Bloodline based on Camazotz","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There were no Mayan or Incan Bloodlines (except one, but it didn't fit what I was looking for - shout out to Deionscribe!) So I just decided to try to make one myself. However, I'm terrible at this, so I put it to you all for feedback.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A little history on Camazotz. </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Mayan Mythology, this evil mythical creature was a gigantic vampire bat said to be the same size as a full grown human male, sometimes even much larger. It would randomly and suddenly attack and suck victims' dry of their blood. Just as a real bat, he only came out during the night to terrorize the local people. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This nightmarish creature reveled in the slaughter of innocent people, and was said to be especially fond of drinking human blood. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This vampiric winged demon was the god of violence, and sacrifice (especially blood sacrifice). </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The gods protected the Mayans from various demons by keeping them enslaved and trapped in the Underworld known as Xibalba. In return for their protection, the gods demanded that the Mayans offer various sacrifices which often included the blood and death of humans. Some of the Mayans eventually revolted against these demands and the cruel laws of the gods. As punishment, the gods unleashed Camazotz out of Xibalba and onto the earth. This mythical monster was said to have destroyed this entire race of Mayans in order that the gods could create another race of humans, a race that would abide by their laws and demands. (he was one of 4 animal monsters that slayed the first race of men)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mayan/Zapotec cult of Camazotz who devoted themselves to this deity would open a vein, fill a wooden or ceramic bowl with their blood, and would offer it up to the Death Bat.</span></span><br /> <br /> [END]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So essentially it'd be a relatively ancient bloodline descended from Camazotz. Mostly based on the idea of a truly monstrous creature that has no place in the modern world. And the difficulties that would provide in a modern vampire game.<br /> <br /> This quote really is what inspired me: &quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They then put them into the House of Bats. There was nothing but bats inside this house, the house of Camazotz, a large animal, whose weapons for killing were like a dry point, and instantly those who came into their presence perished&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blood of Camazotz</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Clan: Gangrel</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nicknames: No idea what's not taken. Horrors? Monsters? Ancients?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disciplines: Protean, Vigor, Resilience, Celerity</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Gift: Unrestrained Aspect</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Blood of Camazotz permanently manifests a Predator\u2019s Aspect for each dot of Blood Potency they possess. For every third dot (3, 6, 9) they instead manifest an Unnatural Aspect. These Aspects are permanently and visibly manifested and will always regenerate or return after a night\u2019s rest if they are forcibly removed. As well, the Camazotz gains her Blood Potency as a bonus to evoke the Monstrous Beast whenever all her Unrestrained Aspects are visible.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Bane: The Thing</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Kindred can never rise above an Average impression with mortals or animals. As well, subtract the Vampire\u2019s Blood Potency as penalties to any non-Intimidation social rolls with humans or animals. High Blood Potency Camazotz often prove incredibly unpopular amongst Kindred due to the risks her Aspects pose to the Masquerade.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Devotion: Shackle the Beast</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Protean 2, Resilience 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3 Vitae </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this Devotion the Camazotz may hide a number of her Unrestrained Aspects equal to her Humanity for a number of hours equal to her resilience. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Merit: Camazotz Form (Not sure how many dots yet)<br /> Protean 3</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This special form granted by the guardians of Xibalba is added to each member of the potential forms of Beast's Skin that members of the Camazotz may take. This form can never be traded out for another, but also doesn't count towards the Camazotz' limit. The Camazotz Form is a large, almost primate looking bat creature, it's face a twisted mess of folds and ridges that amplify sound and scent. The large ears, piercing yellow eyes, chittering clicks, and twitching nose take in all manner of stimuli, allowing for exceptional senses, but what makes the oversized, shaggy, lope limbed form truly terrifying are the finger sized buck teeth in the panting mouth of the beast, each one covered in little serrations and dripping with saliva. Even beyond the unnatural size, this hideous creature could never be mistaken for natural.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength \u25cf\u25cf, Dexterity \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Stamina \u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics (Flight) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Brawl (specified target) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Survival (Bloodtracking) \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense: Greater of Dexterity or Wits</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed: Species Factor 10, flying. 7 galloping</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size: 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attacks: 2L bite, doesn't require a grapple, see below.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits: Acute Senses \u25cf, Bloodhound \u25cf, Distinguished Palate \u25cf, Fighting Finesse \u25cf\u25cf, Fleet of Foot \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Striking Looks (Intimidation) \u25cf\u25cf</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in this form the vampire may use the Bloodhound Merit regardless of their Wits, and the Distinguished Palate Merit ignores the first point of vitae from anyone who isn't of Mayan ancestry, unless the character's natural form has the merit.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Camazotz form always has the benefits of the Extra Sense, Feral Senses, and Wall Crawling Predatory Aspects, even if the character doesn't know those Aspects naturally. If the vampire has at least four dots of Protean, the form's bite is treated as the Horrid Talons Unnatural Aspect. Drawback: Because of the incredible sensory input while in this form, it is incredibly susceptible to overstimulation. Incredibly loud noises, potent smells, and bright lights can disorient or even hurt a Kindred in this form. In loud or bright situations that may not be troubling to the average mortal, the Storyteller may see fit to tag the Camazotz with the first level of Blinded or Deafened, and in areas with heavy scent (pleasant or pungent) Sick may apply. For more drastic, sudden exposures, Frenzy is triggered, penalized by the Kindred's own Protean. On a successful roll (or while resisting) the vampire avoids Frenzy, but is subjected to the more extreme version of the above Tilts.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Primal Fear: The Camazotz Form forces all lesser enemies \u2014 including most humans, spirits of lower Rank, and non-supernatural animals \u2014 to use Down and Dirty combat (see p. 165). If the prey hides in a group of more powerful enemies, resolve the combat as normal. In normal combat, opponents count only their Dexterity or Wits to their Defense; they may not add the appropriate Skill (normally Athletics).</i></span></span></span></span></i></span></span></li> </ul>[The part in Italics are the parts I'm not sure about keeping. Primarily because I'm considering giving the Bloodline access to the Camazotz form immediately upon learning Beast Skin, and then making their<i> default</i> form the Camazotz form at Potency 10. Maybe at Potency 10 they'll get Primal Fear and not before. Some guy helped me with the form. I don't know his name, but I feel I should mention that.]<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 01-13-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:18:12-08:00","id":807029,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also since there are so many Aspects permanently manifested, some (same?) guy also linked me to these homebrew Aspects, so let me know what you think of these also. I don't feel they're necessary but they don't hurt.<br /> <br /> These traits are for Predatory Aspect (Protean \u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Hideous Features: Boney ridges and protuberances grow, and flesh becomes blubbery and flabby. The horrifying look gives +2 to Intimidation, though it tends to penalize other social rolls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Bioluminescence: While the Kindred are able to see in the dark fairly well, sometimes a light is helpful. With this, the vampire\u2019s body produces light from glowing patches of skin equal to a candle. By rapidly flickering them, she can even provide a distraction, causing -2 to any rolls not directed at her.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Frog Tongue: Like a frog or chameleon, the vampire\u2019s tongue is sticky and grasping, capable of shooting out long distances in a flash and jerking back. With a Dexterity + Brawl roll, she can fling her tongue out five feet per dot of Protean and grasp at anything she can reach. If the object is held by someone who doesn\u2019t want to give it up, they can resist with a Dexterity roll. When using this ability, lower specific target penalties by one.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Hardened Skin: A hard shell resembling an armadillo or an armoured insect covers the vampire\u2019s body, providing 1/0 armour.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Sharp Quills: Sticking out of her back and arms, and standing at attention at a whim, these short barb tipped quills provide +2 defense, and anyone making a melee attack against the vampire takes two points of bashing damage</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Mimic Skin: Like an octopus or other boneless animal, the Kindred gains the ability to shift her skin\u2019s texture and colour. So long as she doesn\u2019t move, rolls to notice her are penalized by her Protean dots, though she isn\u2019t invisible.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Alien Senses: Sharks can sense electrical signals, migrating birds seem to rely on magnetism, and vipers can sense their prey\u2019s heat. With this Aspect, the vampire can do much the same.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Sucking Tendrils: The vampire\u2019s skin becomes blubbery and slick, with hands and arms becoming elongated, or new tentacles sprouting,. These appendages grant +1 on any grapple rolls (including to initiate), and treat three successes as exceptional. Suction cups pulse and clamp down, creating hard to break vacuums.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The following are more Bestial traits that might be taken on by the Unnatural Aspect (Protean \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Bone Quills: Hardened protuberances of bone form on the vampire, and for the rest of the scene she can throw these like javelins with a Dexterity + Athletics roll (use Crossbow stats). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Chitinous Plates: Skin hardens and crackles, becoming tough and durable, granting armour with the benefits of chainmail.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Multiple Limbs: A second pair of arms sprout from the vampire\u2019s torso, granting her the ability to hold additional equipment. She could hold a shield and two handed sword and still have a free hand, for example. If she uses all of her arms for the same task, such as climbing a wall or attacking someone, add three to her strength. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Acid Spit: Whether from her mouth or sucking pores, the vampire can shoot a burst of caustic liquid from her body. The damage rating is 0 and it does lethal damage (Aggravated with Claws of the Unholy) with a roll of Dexterity + Athletics + Protean</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Sticky Webbing: The vampire extrudes a silk like substance from her skin, or vomit it out of her orifices. The substance acts as an adhesive on anything she chooses to coat, and can be used in a grapple to subdue an opponent. The durability of the webbing is equal to the Kindred\u2019s Protean.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Cable Sinews: The body of the Kindred twists and stretches, growing taut and ready to strike, with twitching, heightened reflexes. This ability grants +2 to Initiative and Speed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Nauseating Musk: Anyone in ten yards with a sense of smell is subjected to the Sick Tilt. Unnatural as this Aspect is, even Kindred choosing not to breath aren\u2019t immune. Especially keen scented characters may suffer the Grave effect, but for most characters the sickness is Moderate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf Poisonous Venom: The vampire is able to produce a powerful chemical with a Toxicity rating equal to her Protean. When manifesting this aspect, the vampire chooses whether it makes her poisonous or venomous. If she becomes poisonous, the substance secreted through her skin only deals bashing damage, but affects anyone that she touches. If she becomes venomous, then her fangs become able to deliver her toxin. Whichever form it takes, it deals damage once every turn in hectic situations like combat, or once every minute otherwise.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:38:47-08:00","id":807042,"title":"","content":"The layout could use work. And I suspect there may be some grammatical errors that may need correction. Plus, I might have a few points to make with regards to their Bloodline Gift and Bane. But all things considered, I am actually liking this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You created a <i>really </i>vicious monster there. And I say that in a very positive way.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bloodline Gift: Unrestrained Aspect</b><br /> The Camazotz permanently manifest a Predator\u2019s Aspect for each dot of Blood Potency they possess. For every third dot (3, 6, 9) they instead manifest an Unnatural Aspect. These Aspects are permanently and visibly manifested and will always regenerate or return after a night\u2019s rest if they are forcibly removed. As well the Camazotz gains her Blood Potency as a bonus to evoke the Monstrous Beast whenever all her Unrestrained Aspects are visible.<br /> <br /> At Blood Potency 10 the Kindred becomes the Camazotz Form. </div> </div> </div>It seems a bit extreme, at first glance. An alternative take would be to make it additional adaptations the vampire can invoke via Predatory Aspect equal to Blood Potency. Which would give them three additional Unnatural Aspects if you somehow reach Blood Potency 10. But I think this version is pretty thematic with the Camazoztz. The Camazotz Form, meanwhile, could be an exclusive Devotion perhaps? One that the Gangrel can shapeshift to with (at least) 3 Vitae? I don't know.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I really wonder how a confrontation between an Elder Camazotz and an Elder Bak-Ra (specifically my take on them) would turn out. I know it would definitely be messy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bloodline Bane: The Thing</b><br /> The Kindred can never rise above an Average impression with mortals or animals. As well, subtract the Vampire\u2019s Blood Potency as penalties to any non-Intimidation social rolls with humans or animals. Finally, members of this Bloodline may never learn Majesty, Nightmare, or Dominate as their nature compels them to resolve confrontations with their claws and nothing else. </div> </div> </div>Not sure about barring Majesty, Nightmare, or Dominate. Especially if a Gangrel who joins the bloodline might have at least a dot or two in them. Maybe scrap that? As for the social penalty based on Blood Potency, perhaps you can reduce it to being &quot;half the vampire's Blood Potency (rounded up)&quot;. According to saibot, Bloodline Banes shouldn't be <i>too</i> restrictive, even if they should be scaled somewhat according to the benefit of the Gift.<br /> <br /> I got a suggestion, though. How about a Disquiet-like effect as part of the Bane? Like, perhaps, the Predatory Aura leeches out from the Camazotz's very being even when he's not intentionally using it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Also since there are so many Aspects permanently manifested, some (same?) guy also linked me to these homebrew Aspects, so let me know what you think of these also. I don't feel they're necessary but they don't hurt.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. They only hurt on whoever they're used against.<br /> <br /> Lol. Couldn't resist. But I am definitely saving that list of adaptations for future reference.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T08:47:17-08:00","id":807047,"title":"","content":"I'll try to clean it up and respond when I get home from work tonight, but thanks for the feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:27:14-08:00","id":807865,"title":"","content":"Hi Amravanti. <br /> <br /> <br /> I liked how you fleshed them out. <br /> As mayaist I also made Camazotz bloodline for a game i ran. i made it a gangrel/nosferatu bloodline, the original data is lost - so i have to recite from memory. <br /> <br /> Their bloodline weakness(pre 2ed) was a mix of the nosferatu(their face and body twist\u00b4s into a bat like apperance, still monstrous - but as they also where making the sacrifce deals with the humans - i didn\u00b4t want them to have the mechanical drawback) one and the gangrel(no 10 again on mental attributes).<br /> <br /> They used Protean, Nightmare, Vigor, and depended on their parrentclan: Animalism or Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> I gave them a bunch of devotion with goal to become a bipedal terryfing man-bat-monster. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}